# 2026-08-17 22:37:23.329135
+Implement ONLY the next course schedule validation milestone.
+
+Follow AGENTS.md and PROJECT_SPEC.md.
+
+Modify ONLY:
+
+backend/app/schemas/course.py
+
+The SQLAlchemy model and Course API router are read-only references and MUST NOT be modified.
+
+GOAL
+
+Add strict HH:MM 24-hour time validation to:
+
+CourseMeeting.start_time
+CourseMeeting.end_time
+
+Keep both fields typed as str.
+
+Do NOT change them to datetime.time because the schedule is stored in PostgreSQL JSONB and I want the existing JSON serialization/storage behavior to remain unchanged.
+
+Current relevant schema is approximately:
+
+class CourseMeeting(BaseModel):
+    days: list[Literal[
+        "monday",
+        "tuesday",
+        "wednesday",
+        "thursday",
+        "friday",
+        "saturday",
+        "sunday",
+    ]]
+    start_time: str
+    end_time: str
+    location: str | None = None
+
+Use Pydantic v2 validation.
+
+Import field_validator from pydantic.
+
+Add a validator to CourseMeeting that validates BOTH:
+
+start_time
+end_time
+
+Requirements:
+
+- Value must be exactly HH:MM.
+- Use 24-hour time.
+- Hours must be 00 through 23.
+- Minutes must be 00 through 59.
+- Require two-digit hours and two-digit minutes.
+- "14:00" is valid.
+- "09:30" is valid.
+- "00:00" is valid.
+- "23:59" is valid.
+- "9:30" is invalid.
+- "24:00" is invalid.
+- "14:60" is invalid.
+- "2pm" is invalid.
+- "14:00:00" is invalid.
+
+Prefer using datetime.strptime(value, "%H:%M") combined with an exact-format check rather than creating complicated custom parsing logic.
+
+The validator MUST return the original string so the resulting model still contains:
+
+"start_time": "14:00"
+
+rather than a datetime/time object.
+
+Do NOT yet validate:
+
+- whether end_time is after start_time
+- timezone values
+- duplicate days
+- overlapping meetings
+- empty meeting lists
+- schedule recurrence
+
+Do NOT:
+
+- modify backend/app/models/course.py
+- modify backend/app/api/v1/courses.py
+- modify any other file
+- create migrations
+- run Alembic
+- change database schema
+- change JSONB storage
+- change existing weekday validation
+- refactor unrelated code
+- create new files
+- commit changes
+
+Make the smallest possible change.
+
+After applying the edit, show the Git diff for backend/app/schemas/course.py and STOP.
+
+Do not merely show proposed code. APPLY THE EDIT TO DISK.

