+- The user must be able to scroll through ALL remaining items.
+- Do not discard items after the fifth item.
+
+For example, if Upcoming Work contains 12 assignments, the first 5 should fit in the visible area and the user should be able to scroll inside the section to see assignments 6 through 12.
+
+Do NOT simply use:
+
+upcoming.slice(0, 5)
+
+because that would hide the remaining items.
+
+Render the complete collection inside a height-constrained scrollable container.
+
+IMPLEMENTATION
+
+Prefer simple Tailwind/CSS such as:
+
+overflow-y-auto
+
+with an appropriate max-height based on the existing item height.
+
+If the project already uses the shadcn ScrollArea component, it is fine to use it.
+
+Do not install a new dependency solely for this feature.
+
+Scrolling should work with:
+- mouse wheel
+- trackpad
+- touch devices
+
+Preserve:
+- current cards
+- current typography
+- current spacing as much as possible
+- current colors
+- current responsive layout
+- current dark mode behavior
+- current empty states
+
+BACKEND / DATA CHECK
+
