+Read AGENTS.md and PROJECT_SPEC.md before making changes.
+
+I like the current Academic Assistant dashboard layout and design. Do NOT redesign or restructure the dashboard.
+
+I want to improve the dashboard typography.
+
+## Goals
+
+1. Increase the overall text sizes slightly.
+2. Make important text and headings bolder/more prominent.
+3. Change the application font to a softer, friendlier modern font.
+4. Preserve the existing clean academic/productivity aesthetic.
+
+## Font
+
+Change the primary application font to **DM Sans**.
+
+Use the recommended Next.js font-loading approach with `next/font/google`.
+
+Do not load the font using an external CSS `@import`.
+
+If the application already has a centralized font configuration in the root layout, update that implementation rather than adding dashboard-specific font loading.
+
+The font should apply consistently across the application, not just to one individual dashboard component.
+
+Use appropriate available font weights, including enough support for:
+
+* normal body text
+* medium text
+* semibold text
+* bold headings
+
+Do not add an unnecessary font dependency.
+
+## Dashboard Typography
+
+Increase typography sizes moderately.
+
+Do NOT make everything dramatically larger.
+
+The goal is improved readability and visual hierarchy.
+
+### Main Dashboard Heading
+
+Make the main "Dashboard" heading more prominent.
+
+Target approximately:
+
+* text-3xl on smaller screens
+* text-4xl on larger screens
+* font-bold
+
+Keep responsive behavior.
+
+### Dashboard Section Titles
+
+Examples:
+
+* Upcoming Work
+* Next Exam
+* Next Project
+* other existing dashboard section headings
+
+Make these slightly larger and bolder.
+
+Target approximately:
+
+* text-lg or text-xl
+* font-semibold or font-bold
+
+Choose whichever fits the existing layout best.
+
+### Assignment / Exam / Project Titles
+
+Make item titles slightly larger and more prominent.
+
+For example:
+
+* upcoming assignment titles
+* exam titles
+* project titles
+
+Target approximately:
+
+* text-base or text-lg
+* font-semibold
+
+They should visually stand out from metadata.
+
+### Course Names
+
+Course names should remain secondary information but should be easier to read.
+
+Increase them slightly if necessary.
+
+Use approximately:
+
+* text-sm or text-base
+* font-medium
+* text-muted-foreground
+
+The course name should remain visually subordinate to the assignment/exam/project title.
+
+### Metadata
+
+Examples:
+
+* assignment type
+* due dates
+* counts
+* other supporting information
+
+Keep metadata visually secondary.
+
+Do not make every piece of text bold.
+
+Maintain a clear hierarchy:
+
+Page heading
+↓
+Section heading
+↓
+Assignment / Exam / Project title
+↓
+Course name
+↓
+Metadata
+
+## Cards
+
+Do not redesign the cards.
+
+Preserve:
+
+* existing card layout
+* borders
+* spacing
+* colors
+* scrolling behavior
+* dashboard grid
+* responsive behavior
+* dark mode
+
+If slightly increasing padding or vertical spacing is necessary to accommodate the larger typography cleanly, make only small adjustments.
+
+Do not substantially increase card sizes.
+
+## Upcoming Work Scrolling
+
+Preserve the existing scrollable Upcoming Work behavior.
+
+The section should still show approximately 5 items before requiring internal scrolling.
+
+Because text sizes are increasing, verify that the existing max-height still provides a good approximately-five-item visible area.
+
+Adjust the max-height only if necessary.
+
+Do NOT truncate the upcoming list.
+
+All upcoming items must remain accessible through scrolling.
+
+## Responsive Design
+
+Make sure the typography scales appropriately.
+
+Avoid oversized text on mobile.
+
+The dashboard should remain readable on:
+
+* desktop
+* laptop
+* tablet
+* mobile
+
+## Dark Mode
+
+Verify that DM Sans and the typography changes work correctly in both light and dark mode.
+
+Do not change the existing color scheme as part of this task.
+
+## Important Constraints
+
+Do NOT:
+
+* redesign the dashboard
+* change the dashboard information architecture
+* modify backend code
+* modify API calls
+* change API contracts
+* remove existing functionality
+* remove the Upcoming Work scrolling behavior
+* add unnecessary dependencies
+* add decorative fonts
+* use an overly playful font
+* make every piece of text bold
+* modify unrelated pages unnecessarily
+
+The goal is a typography refinement, not a dashboard redesign.
+
+## Validation
+
+After making the changes:
+
+1. Run npm run lint.
+2. Run the existing build/type validation.
+3. Fix errors caused by the changes.
+4. Verify the dashboard visually remains responsive.
+5. Verify the Upcoming Work scroll behavior still works.
+6. Verify light and dark mode typography.
+
+At the end summarize:
+
+* files changed
+* how DM Sans was configured
+* typography sizes/weights changed
+* whether the font applies globally or only to the dashboard
+* whether Upcoming Work max-height needed adjustment
+* validation commands run
+
+Only implement the typography/font changes described above.
+

