# 2026-08-19 21:58:17.457263
+Read AGENTS.md and PROJECT_SPEC.md before making changes.
+
+Modify the Academic Assistant backend dashboard API so the dashboard can return ALL upcoming exams and ALL upcoming projects, not just the single next exam and single next project.
+
+IMPORTANT:
+Do not remove or break the existing next_exam and next_project fields yet. Keep them for backward compatibility.
+
+GOAL
+
+Add two new dashboard response fields:
+
+- upcoming_exams
+- upcoming_projects
+
+Both should be lists of assignment objects using the same assignment response schema already used by the dashboard.
+
+BACKEND BEHAVIOR
+
+For upcoming_exams:
+
+Return all future assignments for the authenticated user where assignment_type represents an exam.
+
+Requirements:
+- only assignments owned by the authenticated user through their courses
+- due_at must be in the future relative to the same "now" logic already used by the dashboard
+- sort ascending by due_at so the next exam is first
+
+For upcoming_projects:
+
+Return all future assignments for the authenticated user where assignment_type represents a project.
+
+Requirements:
+- only assignments owned by the authenticated user through their courses
+- due_at must be in the future
+- sort ascending by due_at so the next project is first
+
+Before writing the query, inspect the existing Assignment model/schema and the current dashboard implementation to confirm the actual assignment_type values used for exams and projects.
+
+Do not invent new enum/type values.
+
+QUERY DESIGN
+
+Avoid doing unnecessary duplicate queries.
+
+Prefer this pattern where practical:
+
+1. Query all upcoming exams into upcoming_exams.
+2. Set:
+   next_exam = upcoming_exams[0] if upcoming_exams else None
+
+3. Query all upcoming projects into upcoming_projects.
+4. Set:
+   next_project = upcoming_projects[0] if upcoming_projects else None
+
+This should replace separate `.first()` queries if that reduces duplicate work cleanly.
+
+SCHEMA CHANGES
+
+Update backend/app/schemas/dashboard.py.
+
+Add:
+
+upcoming_exams: list[AssignmentResponse]
+upcoming_projects: list[AssignmentResponse]
+
+Use the existing assignment schema already used by the dashboard.
+
+Do not create a duplicate assignment schema unless absolutely necessary.
+
+Keep these existing fields:
+
+next_exam
+next_project
+
+unless the current schema uses different exact names/types.
+
+RESPONSE
+
+Update the dashboard response construction to include:
+
+upcoming_exams=upcoming_exams
+upcoming_projects=upcoming_projects
+
+Preserve all existing dashboard fields and behavior.
+
+COURSE NAME
+
+Do not change the backend response to embed course_name in each assignment unless the existing dashboard schema already does so.
+
+The frontend can continue resolving course_id using its existing course data.
+
+SECURITY
+
+Preserve the existing authenticated-user ownership boundaries.
+
+Do not return assignments belonging to other users.
+
+CONSTRAINTS
+
+Do NOT:
+- modify unrelated endpoints
+- change assignment extraction logic
+- change database models
+- create migrations
+- change API paths
+- remove next_exam
+- remove next_project
+- change unrelated dashboard fields
+- add unnecessary dependencies
+
+VALIDATION
+
+After making the changes:
+
+1. Run the relevant backend import/type validation already used by this project.
+2. If practical, run an existing dashboard test or start-up validation.
+3. Verify that DashboardResponse includes:
+   - upcoming_exams
+   - upcoming_projects
+4. Verify next_exam is the first upcoming exam or None.
+5. Verify next_project is the first upcoming project or None.
+6. Verify the lists are sorted by due_at ascending.
+7. Verify user ownership filtering remains intact.
+
+At the end summarize:
+- files changed
+- query changes
+- schema changes
+- actual assignment_type values used
+- whether duplicate next_exam/next_project queries were removed
+- validation commands run
+
+Only implement the backend dashboard changes described above.

